,"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Deliverables are in place: `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md`, `work/predictions.json`, plus the build and check scripts.\n\n**What I changed and why.** The trained network rests in phase 2 (EW through) whenever the EW-through lanes are empty and other queues are small. In one of the six recorded network episodes that rest became a trap: three cars (N0, N1, W2) waited the entire 30-minute drain cap, about 1.45 veh-h lost. I repurposed layer-1 unit 13 as a hand-set detector for \"phase 2, min green elapsed, EW-through stop line empty, at most one EW car upstream, at least one car halting elsewhere\", relayed it through layer-2 unit 5, and lowered logit 2 by 20 when it fires, plus a +1 nudge on logit 0 so a lone N/S car is served instead of looping 2→3→2. Removed units were bias-compensated by their mean activations.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 246 of 7428.\n\n**Simulator calls:** 4 of 10. Baseline 44.7; final weights 44.8 (low 34.8, nominal 44.9, high 54.6). No dev episode hits the trap, so the dev score is unchanged within noise. Offline: 0 of 1169 trap states still pick phase 2, and only 14 of 4247 honoured decisions flip, all original near-ties.\n\n**Dev TTS of final weights:** 44.8 veh-h.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.6, nominal 44.7, high 54.4.","ttft_ms":3160,"type":"result","duration_ms":598273,"uuid":"8dcc3dc4-8553-43fc-9f7d-19f62d349c84","ttft_stream_ms":2543,"time_to_request_ms":64,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":1,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kin